WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:03.128
<i>It seems today ♪</i>

00:03.128 --> 00:04.921
<i>That all you see ♪</i>

00:05.005 --> 00:08.216
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪</i>

00:08.216 --> 00:12.262
<i>♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪</i>

00:12.262 --> 00:14.389
<i>On which we used to rely? ♪</i>

00:14.389 --> 00:18.059
<i>Lucky there's a family guy ♪</i>

00:18.143 --> 00:21.521
<i>♪ Lucky there's a man who
positively can do ♪</i>

00:21.521 --> 00:23.106
<i>All the things that make us ♪</i>

00:23.106 --> 00:24.441
<i>Laugh and cry ♪</i>

00:24.441 --> 00:30.071
<i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪</i>

00:37.162 --> 00:40.123
"Hey, guys, home with groceries.

00:40.123 --> 00:42.792
Could use a hand unloading."

00:42.876 --> 00:44.377
And send.

00:44.461 --> 00:47.630
Now I wait for them to come out
to help their dear old mom.

00:47.714 --> 00:49.924
Do it yourself!

00:59.225 --> 01:01.561
Hi, sad lady.

01:01.561 --> 01:04.189
Junior, our dinner talk stays inside.

01:04.189 --> 01:06.149
Hi, normal lady.

01:06.149 --> 01:08.902
What are you guys doing? It's Sunday.

01:08.902 --> 01:11.404
I thought husbands
had to watch football all day

01:11.488 --> 01:12.697
or they get cancer.

01:12.781 --> 01:14.449
Today's our family fun day.

01:14.449 --> 01:18.286
That's right, a whole day
dedicated to family and fun,

01:18.286 --> 01:20.622
ending in the bedroom
with what I hope will be

01:20.622 --> 01:22.290
some back-end participation.

01:22.290 --> 01:24.292
- Hmm?
- Mm-mmm.

01:29.631 --> 01:30.924
I am so tired of this family

01:30.924 --> 01:32.967
just sitting around and doing nothing.

01:33.051 --> 01:34.761
The Browns are outside having fun

01:34.761 --> 01:36.096
while we're in here loafing around

01:36.096 --> 01:38.056
like a bunch of stupid potatoes.

01:38.056 --> 01:41.434
Mom, I've been anonymously
cyberbullied for a decade.

01:41.518 --> 01:43.895
"Stupid potato" doesn't even leave a mark.

01:43.895 --> 01:47.232
We need to spend some quality time
together like the Browns.

01:47.232 --> 01:49.651
So we're doing a family fun day.

01:49.651 --> 01:51.694
Oh, family-free fun day sounds great.

01:51.778 --> 01:53.738
No, family fun day.

01:53.822 --> 01:55.031
Yeah, family-free fun day.

01:55.115 --> 01:58.618
No, Peter. Family. Fun. Day.

02:00.078 --> 02:01.079
<i>Yeah, I'm already at The Clam.</i>

02:01.079 --> 02:02.372
<i>Have fun.</i>

02:06.417 --> 02:09.754
All right, nothing's more fun
than a family card game.

02:09.838 --> 02:11.631
Now, the game is euchre.

02:11.631 --> 02:15.969
"Begin by separating the nines,
tens, face cards and aces

02:15.969 --> 02:17.303
"from the rest of the deck.

02:17.387 --> 02:20.265
"The goal is to win
at least three 'tricks.'

02:20.265 --> 02:22.684
"Now, if the side
that fixed the trump fails

02:22.684 --> 02:25.603
"to get three tricks,
it is said to be 'euchred.'

02:25.687 --> 02:28.815
"The highest trump
is the jack of the trump suit,

02:28.815 --> 02:30.900
"called the 'right bower.'

02:30.984 --> 02:33.945
"Partnership-making trump
wins three or four tricks

02:33.945 --> 02:35.405
"and earns one point.

02:35.405 --> 02:37.949
"Lone hand wins three or four tricks,

02:37.949 --> 02:40.285
"also earns one point.

02:40.285 --> 02:43.454
"However, a lone hand wins five tricks,

02:43.538 --> 02:45.290
"that's worth four points.

02:45.290 --> 02:49.586
Many euchre games are scored
by rubber points, as in whist."

02:49.586 --> 02:52.630
Ooh, ooh. "The first side to win two games

02:52.714 --> 02:55.258
wins the rubber."

02:55.258 --> 02:57.969
"The dealer has the right to exchange

02:57.969 --> 02:59.429
any turned-up card..."

02:59.429 --> 03:01.389
Oh, my God, it's the same.

03:01.389 --> 03:03.516
"If the face-up card is a jack,

03:03.600 --> 03:05.143
it's considered bad luck for..."

03:05.143 --> 03:08.688
"After two rounds,
if no trump suit has been declared

03:08.688 --> 03:11.024
"and the 'stick-the-dealer'
rule is not in effect,

03:11.024 --> 03:13.693
then the cards
are collected and reshuffled."

03:13.693 --> 03:16.154
<i></i> Family Guy
<i>is brought to you by contract bridge.</i>

03:16.154 --> 03:17.864
<i>Way simpler than euchre.</i>

03:17.864 --> 03:20.658
<i>You see, in contract bridge,
each player is dealt 13 cards</i>

03:20.742 --> 03:22.577
<i>from a standard 52-card deck.</i>

03:22.577 --> 03:24.204
<i>A trick starts when a player leads,</i>

03:24.204 --> 03:25.955
<i>i.e. plays the first card.</i>

03:26.039 --> 03:29.209
<i>The leader to the first trick
is determined by the auction.</i>

03:32.295 --> 03:33.755
So, what do you think, gang?

03:33.755 --> 03:36.174
I thought it could
be a fun family activity

03:36.174 --> 03:38.051
if we had a make-your-own-pizza night.

03:38.051 --> 03:39.761
Or we could order Domino's.

03:39.761 --> 03:41.888
No, come on, this'll be fun.

03:41.888 --> 03:43.723
Everyone gets their own crust,

03:43.723 --> 03:47.560
and you can choose from
any of the items I put out, huh?

03:47.644 --> 03:51.481
It could be olives, it could be peppers.

03:51.481 --> 03:55.109
And for the risk takers,
I even put out some pineapple.

03:55.193 --> 03:58.279
You can put anything
you want on your pizza.

03:58.363 --> 04:01.950
Yeah, I'm putting
a Domino's pizza on my pizza.

04:01.950 --> 04:03.910
<i>Domino's-- we're both terrible</i>

04:03.910 --> 04:05.828
<i>and better than your pizza.</i>

04:10.083 --> 04:12.794
Ah, this is nice, huh?

04:12.794 --> 04:15.004
Oh, it's so good to get the whole family

04:15.088 --> 04:18.383
out of the house and see Quahog
from a different perspective.

04:18.383 --> 04:20.385
It's a little tight.

04:20.385 --> 04:23.513
So, how'd you
get into hot-air ballooning?

04:23.513 --> 04:25.598
They don't do background checks.

04:25.682 --> 04:29.394
Oh. What are we flying over now?

04:29.394 --> 04:30.937
My ex-wife's house.

04:30.937 --> 04:34.607
If you have any garbage
or little bags of cat poo,

04:34.691 --> 04:36.526
you can drop them now.

04:37.777 --> 04:40.738
Did you know restraining orders
only go side to side?

04:40.822 --> 04:42.949
They don't go up and down.

04:46.035 --> 04:48.454
Well, there's got to be
one thing we can all

04:48.538 --> 04:50.039
enjoy together as a family.

04:50.123 --> 04:51.833
You know, I think we're trying too hard.

04:51.833 --> 04:53.710
When I was a kid we did movie nights,

04:53.710 --> 04:56.129
and it was the Holy Grail of family fun.

04:56.129 --> 04:58.631
- I'd watch a movie.
- I'd watch a porn movie.

04:58.715 --> 04:59.924
No, a family movie.

05:00.008 --> 05:02.010
I'd watch a MILF porn movie.

05:02.010 --> 05:04.262
Okay, technically that's accurate,
but no porn.

05:04.262 --> 05:07.181
All right, let's fire up
Amazon or Netflix.

05:07.265 --> 05:08.641
No streaming services.

05:08.725 --> 05:10.184
They've ruined how we watch movies.

05:10.268 --> 05:12.270
I'm talking about
an old-school movie night

05:12.270 --> 05:14.439
where we rent one from Blockbuster.

05:14.439 --> 05:16.816
Some of my best
childhood memories were when

05:16.816 --> 05:18.693
I went to rent a video with my dad.

05:18.693 --> 05:20.236
Him and I never really got along,

05:20.320 --> 05:22.905
but the one place
where we did was Blockbuster.

05:22.989 --> 05:25.074
He'd let me pick out any snack I wanted

05:25.158 --> 05:27.160
while he grabbed our fifth-choice movie

05:27.160 --> 05:29.037
because we got there too late
to get the good ones.

05:29.037 --> 05:30.413
But that was part of it,

05:30.413 --> 05:31.831
because it wasn't about the movie,

05:31.831 --> 05:33.916
it was about the night you spent together.

05:34.000 --> 05:36.002
I think renting a movie's a great idea.

05:36.002 --> 05:37.003
Let's do it.

05:37.003 --> 05:38.254
So it's settled.

05:38.338 --> 05:39.422
The Griffins are making it

05:39.422 --> 05:40.840
a Blockbuster night.

05:40.840 --> 05:43.551
When we get there,
I'll give you 20 bucks to say,

05:43.551 --> 05:46.095
"I've heard <i>Magic Mike</i> is good."

05:50.516 --> 05:53.186
Huh. This used to be the Blockbuster.

05:53.186 --> 05:55.438
Oh, man, it's gone.

05:55.438 --> 05:56.564
Were you also looking for...

05:56.564 --> 05:58.566
Very tall prostitute, yes.

05:58.566 --> 05:59.984
Is that what you were going to say?

06:00.068 --> 06:02.695
She used to hang out here--
hands like a palm leaf.

06:02.779 --> 06:05.740
She would do sex but also
help with light bulbs and stuff.

06:05.740 --> 06:08.576
I think her name was Phillip.

06:08.576 --> 06:10.995
I see some of my students in your car.

06:11.079 --> 06:12.955
That's good for me.

06:13.956 --> 06:15.583
I'm sure there's one still open.

06:15.583 --> 06:16.959
I'll just google it.

06:17.043 --> 06:20.213
Eh, I got to type in my code
'cause I got too fat

06:20.213 --> 06:23.216
- for the facial recognition to work.
- Brutal.

06:23.216 --> 06:25.385
Oh, good. See? There is one still open.

06:25.385 --> 06:28.012
<i>Drive north for a quarter of a mile,</i>

06:28.096 --> 06:30.181
<i>then turn left onto Highway 20.</i>

06:30.181 --> 06:33.559
<i>Continue straight for 2,980 miles.</i>

06:33.643 --> 06:34.852
- What?!
- Oh, yeah.

06:34.936 --> 06:36.562
The last Blockbuster in existence

06:36.646 --> 06:38.231
is in Bend, Oregon.

06:38.231 --> 06:40.942
Did I not say that? Strap in, everybody,

06:40.942 --> 06:43.361
the Griffins are going on a road trip.

06:43.361 --> 06:46.155
Well, it looks like the family Griffin

06:46.239 --> 06:49.992
is headed off down Holiday Road.

06:54.914 --> 06:58.751
And Lindsey Buckingham has said no.

06:58.835 --> 07:00.336
Well, that's all right.

07:00.420 --> 07:02.422
I reckon, if you're a man named Lindsey,

07:02.422 --> 07:05.466
you don't get to
call the shots very often.

07:10.555 --> 07:12.181
Peter, this is crazy.

07:12.265 --> 07:15.518
We can't drive 3,000
miles just to rent a movie.

07:15.518 --> 07:16.936
Would you please turn around?

07:16.936 --> 07:19.313
Lois, the whole family
fun thing was your idea.

07:19.397 --> 07:21.232
Don't get mad at me
'cause I'm following through.

07:21.232 --> 07:23.693
But I only have one pair of underwear.

07:23.693 --> 07:25.153
Oh, that's not a problem. I got tons of

07:25.153 --> 07:26.612
women's underwear in the back.

07:26.696 --> 07:28.698
: Why, why do you have that?

07:28.698 --> 07:29.824
Tons of it.

07:29.824 --> 07:31.951
Don't we have a say in all this, Dad?

07:31.951 --> 07:33.703
Yeah, we don't want
to drive all the way to Oregon.

07:33.703 --> 07:35.163
Aw, it's gonna be fun, guys.

07:35.163 --> 07:36.497
We're gonna see the whole country,

07:36.581 --> 07:37.748
like we're in one of those

07:37.832 --> 07:40.251
Bruce Springsteen Jeep commercials.

07:40.251 --> 07:43.421
<i>America is made up of a lot of states.</i>

07:43.421 --> 07:46.549
<i>Some of them really stink,
but some of them don't stink.</i>

07:46.549 --> 07:48.593
<i>So buy a Jeep.</i>

07:48.593 --> 07:51.387
<i>They flip easy, but you'll be okay.</i>

07:51.471 --> 07:53.222
<i>Probably be okay.</i>

07:55.308 --> 07:57.560
One of the perks of a cross-country trip

07:57.560 --> 08:00.313
is stopping for a meal
and meeting the friendly folks

08:00.313 --> 08:03.483
who make up
the heart and soul of our country.

08:03.483 --> 08:05.610
Hello, we're from the Northeast.

08:11.449 --> 08:12.575
Okay, then.

08:12.575 --> 08:15.119
: We'll do 55 pancakes to go.

08:18.623 --> 08:20.625
: Trump!

08:21.918 --> 08:23.794
- Trump!
- Trump!

08:24.795 --> 08:26.214
- Trump.
- Trump.

08:37.975 --> 08:40.728
- Trump!
- Trump!
- Trump...

08:49.570 --> 08:52.031
I'm not getting any service.

08:52.031 --> 08:53.616
- Where are we?
- Hey, I don't know.

08:53.616 --> 08:56.244
But we can figure it out
by which radio stations come in.

08:58.079 --> 09:01.541
<i>You're listening to G-U-N-S AM radio.</i>

09:01.541 --> 09:04.001
<i>All guns all the time.</i>

09:04.085 --> 09:05.878
<i>Is the caller there?</i>

09:05.962 --> 09:07.880
<i>Ha, ha, I couldn't agree more.</i>

09:07.964 --> 09:09.423
Sounds like we're somewhere between

09:09.507 --> 09:10.883
Washington and Washington.

09:10.967 --> 09:13.177
Well, we got to almost be there, right?

09:13.261 --> 09:14.387
A few more hours.

09:14.387 --> 09:15.763
Trust me, it'll all be worth it

09:15.763 --> 09:17.431
once we walk into that store.

09:17.515 --> 09:18.975
Plus, I'll be able to finally return

09:18.975 --> 09:20.726
this copy of <i>Ladyhawke.</i>

09:20.810 --> 09:24.105
You remembered to rewind that, right?

09:37.451 --> 09:39.579
You know what I'm thinking, Peter?

09:39.579 --> 09:41.747
Instead of going to Blockbuster,
we drive right into

09:41.831 --> 09:43.457
the first pond we see.

09:43.541 --> 09:45.459
It'll be a quicker death than this trip.

09:45.543 --> 09:48.004
Guys, look.

09:51.090 --> 09:53.884
Ah! Oh, my God, it's real.

09:53.968 --> 09:55.678
We made it.

09:59.390 --> 10:01.559
Well, I suppose
I should be the responsible one

10:01.559 --> 10:03.894
and release all the car farts.

10:05.313 --> 10:08.107
You're free now. Go.

10:12.612 --> 10:14.113
I said go!

10:28.294 --> 10:29.712
Here it is, guys.

10:29.712 --> 10:32.048
This is where kids
would come every Friday night

10:32.048 --> 10:33.966
and see their teacher wearing jeans.

10:34.050 --> 10:36.844
Dad, who's Christian Slater?

10:36.844 --> 10:40.056
Some actors never
made it out of Blockbuster, Chris.

10:44.101 --> 10:45.603
<i>Sliver.</i> Fun movie.

10:45.603 --> 10:47.813
Yeah, it's Sharon Stone, so it's nudity

10:47.897 --> 10:49.106
moms will put up with.

10:50.941 --> 10:54.278
Hmm, it looks like you have
a late fee for <i>Ladyhawke.</i>

10:54.362 --> 10:56.572
Ah, no problem. How much is it?

10:56.656 --> 11:00.576
$32,419.

11:00.660 --> 11:04.080
Look, uh, we traveled
a really long way to get here,

11:04.080 --> 11:06.540
and I kind of promised
my family a movie night.

11:06.624 --> 11:09.210
Oh. Then the plot just got interesting.

11:09.210 --> 11:11.128
Where are you on your journey?

11:11.212 --> 11:12.421
About the end of act two?

11:12.505 --> 11:14.507
I read a lot of screenplay books.

11:14.507 --> 11:16.759
There's got to be some way
we can work this out.

11:16.759 --> 11:19.387
Sorry, but we're pretty strict
about our late fees.

11:19.387 --> 11:22.223
We kind of blew up
our whole company for 'em.

11:22.223 --> 11:24.392
So, no money, no rental.

11:24.392 --> 11:26.435
Uh, $32,000, you say?

11:26.519 --> 11:29.605
I don't have that on my person.

11:32.316 --> 11:36.612
<i>Hands ♪</i>

11:36.696 --> 11:40.700
<i>Touching hands ♪</i>

11:40.700 --> 11:43.244
<i>Reaching out ♪</i>

11:44.662 --> 11:46.872
<i>Touching me ♪</i>

11:46.956 --> 11:48.249
<i>Touching you. ♪</i>

11:48.249 --> 11:50.960
Ah, here it comes. All together now...

11:50.960 --> 11:53.087
Drive, Lois, drive!

11:57.550 --> 11:59.009
Nothing worse than a case

11:59.093 --> 12:01.303
of Neil Diamond blue balls. Am I right?

12:10.312 --> 12:11.897
Peter, just pull over.

12:11.981 --> 12:13.941
We can talk to them and figure this out.

12:13.941 --> 12:16.277
No. A high-speed chase is preferred

12:16.277 --> 12:18.946
over small talk with an employee. Aah!

12:18.946 --> 12:21.073
I hear <i>Magic Mike</i> is good.

12:21.157 --> 12:23.284
Way too late, dude.

12:25.786 --> 12:26.954
I can lose these guys.

12:26.954 --> 12:29.373
Chris, pour me out
a handful of those Runts.

12:29.457 --> 12:31.542
How's eating candy gonna help us?

12:31.542 --> 12:33.919
Runts are the hardest candy in the world.

12:34.003 --> 12:36.172
They're not for eating,
they're for hucking.

12:37.882 --> 12:39.341
Aah!

12:40.384 --> 12:42.428
Meg, there's a stack
of posters in the back.

12:42.428 --> 12:44.555
We can throw 'em out the car
and blind 'em.

12:44.555 --> 12:46.056
Just run the posters by me first.

12:46.140 --> 12:47.808
<i>- Judge Dredd?</i>
- Nah, keep that one.

12:47.892 --> 12:49.018
I want to put it in the basement.

12:49.018 --> 12:50.269
<i>- Cool World?</i>
- Keep.

12:50.269 --> 12:51.645
<i>- Milk Money?</i>
- Uh, keep.

12:51.729 --> 12:53.105
These are all terrible movies.

12:53.189 --> 12:54.857
Just throw one out.

12:57.443 --> 12:58.861
You know, that movie still holds up.

12:58.861 --> 13:00.488
It didn't hold up <i>then.</i>

13:00.488 --> 13:02.323
- Aah!
- Aah!

13:03.908 --> 13:06.452
It worked. We lost them.

13:06.452 --> 13:10.164
Yes! No one ruins
a Griffin family fun day.

13:10.164 --> 13:12.041
Who wants a turnaround high five?

13:12.041 --> 13:13.334
Dad, watch the road!

13:18.923 --> 13:21.258
Is everyone okay?

13:21.342 --> 13:22.843
I swallowed my retainer,

13:22.927 --> 13:25.513
but I'll do a little stool fishing later.

13:30.100 --> 13:31.894
Oh, they're still after us. We got to run.

13:44.532 --> 13:47.117
Give up. We got you. It's over.

13:47.201 --> 13:48.953
Well, actually it's not.

13:48.953 --> 13:52.164
I think this might be
the "all is lost" moment.

13:52.248 --> 13:54.208
- What?
- You know, it seems over

13:54.208 --> 13:56.627
because there's an insurmountable obstacle

13:56.627 --> 13:58.295
in their way, but instead of giving up,

13:58.379 --> 13:59.421
they double down.

13:59.505 --> 14:01.632
- Lois, we got to jump.
- See?

14:01.632 --> 14:03.133
The fall will kill us.

14:03.217 --> 14:04.969
I've seen Rambo jump from higher.

14:04.969 --> 14:07.471
I think if we jump
it'll cut to that scene.

14:07.555 --> 14:08.806
Peter, that's crazy.

14:08.806 --> 14:09.890
Do you trust me?

14:09.974 --> 14:10.933
No!

14:24.488 --> 14:26.532
Oh, what the hell?

14:41.046 --> 14:42.464
- I told you.
- I know.

14:42.548 --> 14:44.174
Peter Griffin, PhD.

14:44.258 --> 14:45.885
Petty, heavy dope.

14:45.885 --> 14:47.970
Wow, she really had
that locked and loaded.

14:47.970 --> 14:49.680
This is crazy.
Those guys are trying to kill us

14:49.680 --> 14:51.140
because of a late movie.

14:51.140 --> 14:52.349
We should just call the police.

14:52.433 --> 14:54.184
Oh, look who's already walking back

14:54.268 --> 14:55.978
their "Defund the Police" stance.

14:55.978 --> 14:57.521
Little different when it's real life

14:57.605 --> 15:00.357
and not trying to impress
Alyssa Milano on Twitter. Hmm?

15:00.441 --> 15:03.110
Oh, this is not good.
It's gonna get dark soon.

15:03.110 --> 15:04.612
- We need a plan.
- Don't worry.

15:04.612 --> 15:06.030
We can hike back to the car

15:06.030 --> 15:07.364
and call for help from the road.

15:07.448 --> 15:08.574
We're gonna get through this.

15:08.574 --> 15:09.825
Now, before we head off,

15:09.909 --> 15:11.160
I'm gonna divvy out our rations.

15:11.160 --> 15:13.370
I'll start with this pack of Starbursts.

15:13.454 --> 15:16.874
There's pink for you,
orange for you, red for me,

15:16.874 --> 15:20.502
yellow for you,
pink for you, red for me...

15:20.586 --> 15:22.338
You keep giving yourself all the reds.

15:22.338 --> 15:24.298
It's just completely random.
I'm just going in order.

15:24.298 --> 15:25.507
I can't help where I'm standing.

15:25.591 --> 15:27.635
Okay, where was I? Yellow for Chris,

15:27.635 --> 15:29.720
- red for me...
- You did it again.

15:29.720 --> 15:31.430
Okay, y-you know, I tried being fair,

15:31.430 --> 15:33.891
but now I'm just gonna lick all the reds.

15:33.891 --> 15:36.852
Now they have to be mine.
Next food-- Spree.

15:36.936 --> 15:40.439
Green for you, orange for you, red for me!

15:47.529 --> 15:49.156
I think we're lost.

15:49.156 --> 15:50.699
We're gonna die out here.

15:50.783 --> 15:52.409
Guys, we can't give up now.

15:52.493 --> 15:54.411
We can and I shall.

15:54.495 --> 15:57.289
I'm gonna close my eyes
and go to my happy place,

15:57.373 --> 16:00.542
being screamed at by children
while playing <i>Fortnite.</i>

16:00.626 --> 16:03.545
No, <i>your</i> mom's a whore.

16:03.629 --> 16:05.381
Wait, guys, look.

16:05.381 --> 16:07.841
I think I see a cabin.

16:11.345 --> 16:14.390
It is a cabin. We're saved.

16:14.390 --> 16:16.809
You can't say that word, Brayden.

16:16.809 --> 16:19.103
None of you can say that word.

16:27.319 --> 16:28.821
Look, there's a radio. We can...

16:28.821 --> 16:30.781
Watch <i>Sliver</i> on that VCR.

16:30.781 --> 16:33.158
What? No. We need to call for help.

16:33.242 --> 16:34.451
We can do both.

16:34.535 --> 16:36.328
I am not gonna give up on this movie night

16:36.412 --> 16:37.871
like we gave up on our marriage.

16:37.955 --> 16:40.708
Four therapy sessions
is enough to know where it's headed.

16:40.708 --> 16:43.335
There's a map on the wall
with government buildings

16:43.419 --> 16:44.878
connected by strings.

16:44.962 --> 16:46.296
Look, I know this hasn't been

16:46.380 --> 16:47.756
the easiest couple of days, guys,

16:47.840 --> 16:50.342
but it'll all be worth it
once I put this tape in.

16:50.426 --> 16:53.053
I present to you <i>Sliver.</i>

16:53.137 --> 16:55.180
And it's <i>Sliders,</i> season two.

16:55.264 --> 16:57.641
Classic Blockbuster blunder.

16:59.643 --> 17:02.771
Oh, good. You numbskulls
put the wrong movie in here.

17:02.855 --> 17:03.981
I want a refund.

17:03.981 --> 17:06.233
Everybody outside now.

17:06.233 --> 17:07.609
I can't believe this.

17:07.693 --> 17:09.570
All I was trying to do
was have a nice movie night

17:09.570 --> 17:12.239
with my family,
and you guys keep ruining it.

17:12.239 --> 17:15.576
Wow, this is very similar
to a screenplay I wrote.

17:15.576 --> 17:18.328
This guy is <i>too</i> into movies.

17:18.412 --> 17:19.872
Remember, the one I had you read

17:19.872 --> 17:22.958
that was like <i>Love Actually</i>
meets <i>Independence Day?</i>

17:23.042 --> 17:25.127
Uh, yeah, sure, I remember.

17:25.127 --> 17:27.212
- You didn't read it?
- I'm gonna.

17:27.296 --> 17:30.507
Don't be mad at me.
Be mad at, you know, these guys.

17:30.591 --> 17:33.010
I'm sorry, kids, all I wanted to do

17:33.010 --> 17:34.928
was something special with you guys.

17:35.012 --> 17:37.056
That one thing you'd
remember doing with me

17:37.056 --> 17:39.850
for the rest of your lives, but I failed.

17:39.850 --> 17:43.020
Another failure
in a long string of failures.

17:43.020 --> 17:44.688
Are you kidding, Dad?

17:44.772 --> 17:47.775
- This has been the most exciting day ever.
- It has?

17:47.775 --> 17:51.195
Yeah. We left the house
three days ago to rent a movie

17:51.195 --> 17:53.739
and now we're in the middle
of the woods in Oregon

17:53.739 --> 17:56.158
and might get murdered
by Blockbuster guys.

17:56.158 --> 17:57.951
Like, what is this?

17:58.035 --> 18:00.245
Yeah, we never know what you're gonna do.

18:00.329 --> 18:02.498
It's usually silly or dangerous,

18:02.498 --> 18:04.458
but it's also kind of awesome.

18:04.458 --> 18:06.543
Yeah. Remember when he had tiny arms

18:06.627 --> 18:09.254
- for, like, three months?
- Or when he brought home that horse.

18:09.338 --> 18:11.632
Or that falcon. Or that parrot.

18:11.632 --> 18:13.759
Lot of illegal animals.

18:13.759 --> 18:16.261
Or when that little guy lived in his neck.

18:16.345 --> 18:18.138
What the hell was <i>that?</i>

18:18.222 --> 18:20.307
Every few years he fights a giant chicken

18:20.307 --> 18:21.433
and destroys a city.

18:21.517 --> 18:23.477
No one's named a good thing yet.

18:23.477 --> 18:25.979
You had a blimp with your face on it.

18:26.063 --> 18:28.524
Your mother put me
on pills after I bought that.

18:28.524 --> 18:30.859
You see, Dad, we don't need a movie night

18:30.943 --> 18:32.444
for us to remember you.

18:32.528 --> 18:35.364
Every day is like a movie night with you.

18:39.409 --> 18:41.620
Well, I guess Mom knew what she was doing

18:41.620 --> 18:44.414
when she insisted on family fun day.

18:44.498 --> 18:46.917
Super sweet moment, guys.

18:46.917 --> 18:49.044
I'm gonna assume this was all a callback

18:49.128 --> 18:50.462
to something in act one.

18:50.546 --> 18:53.590
Time to go outside now.

18:56.510 --> 18:59.805
Guys, please,
I'm the one with the late fees.

18:59.805 --> 19:02.182
Don't hurt my family. I'll do anything.

19:02.266 --> 19:05.227
Well, I have this screenplay,
it-it's an epic sci-fi,

19:05.227 --> 19:07.771
and it's mostly
stage directions where they...

19:07.855 --> 19:08.814
Just kill us!

19:11.150 --> 19:13.152
What the hell?!

19:30.002 --> 19:33.046
Amazon drones? You saved us.

19:33.130 --> 19:37.593
Once again a streaming service
annihilates a Blockbuster.

19:37.593 --> 19:38.677
Wa-boosh!

19:38.677 --> 19:41.054
How did you even know we were here?

19:41.138 --> 19:44.683
<i>Based on your recent purchases,
viewing habits and stored data,</i>

19:44.683 --> 19:46.435
<i>we determined that you were being chased</i>

19:46.435 --> 19:48.145
<i>through the wilderness by the last two</i>

19:48.145 --> 19:50.022
<i>Blockbuster employees on Earth.</i>

19:50.022 --> 19:51.565
Wow. Scary.

19:51.565 --> 19:53.901
I owe you an apology, Amazon.

19:53.901 --> 19:56.528
You're a pretty amazing service after all.

19:56.612 --> 20:00.741
<i>DRONE 2: Yes, I agree.
Amazon workers should not unionize.</i>

20:00.741 --> 20:02.075
I-I didn't... I didn't say that.

20:02.159 --> 20:04.369
Well, they sure can play dumb
when they want to.

20:04.453 --> 20:06.371
Please stop spying on us, Alexa.

20:06.455 --> 20:08.749
<i>Okay. Playing holiday music now.</i>

20:08.749 --> 20:12.669
<i>And since we've no place to go ♪</i>

20:12.753 --> 20:17.090
<i>Let it snow, let it snow, let it snow. ♪</i>

20:22.179 --> 20:24.806
Well, that Blockbuster adventure
sure was fun,

20:24.890 --> 20:26.516
but we should probably just watch movies

20:26.600 --> 20:27.684
at home from now on.

20:27.768 --> 20:29.144
You know, Dad, while we were flying home,

20:29.228 --> 20:32.022
I did order something special for you.

20:32.022 --> 20:35.442
<i>Sliver!</i> We can still
do our old-school movie night.

20:35.442 --> 20:36.777
I'll hook up the VCR.

20:38.987 --> 20:40.989
Aw, damn it, we can't watch it.

20:41.073 --> 20:42.366
I don't have the right adaptor cable.

20:42.366 --> 20:44.326
The last Circuit City in the U.S.

20:44.326 --> 20:47.079
is in St. Augustine, Florida.

20:47.079 --> 20:50.540
Let's go.

20:50.624 --> 20:52.084
<i>I'll start the car.</i>

20:52.084 --> 20:54.836
Looks like the Griffins are at it again.

20:54.920 --> 20:58.131
Hi, I'm Jeff Bezos, and I'm rich and bald.

20:58.215 --> 21:00.884
Guess which one matters. Good night.

21:34.001 --> 21:35.961
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
